      "content": "helplines just tell you the same scripted stuff. it doesnt change the fact that there is nothing left. i look in the mirror and i don't even recognize the person looking back. it's like the real me died when my career did. i'm just a shell. sometimes i think the world would actually be quieter, just... less cluttered, if i wasn't even here. like it would just be easier for everyone if i just stopped trying.",
